# Trivy findings accepted on purpose, each with its reason. Read by the verifier-image and
# app-image scans in .github/workflows/ci.yml; anything not listed here still fails CI.
# Review when BATFISH_IMAGE (Makefile, Dockerfile.verifier, docker-compose.yml) is bumped:
# a newer Batfish release that ships fixed libraries makes these entries obsolete.
#
# Java libraries shaded inside batfish/allinone's allinone-bundle.jar. They cannot be
# patched without rebuilding Batfish from source. Exposure in Fabloom: the Batfish server
# runs inside a single-tenant sandbox (or on localhost / a compose-internal network for the
# local backend), is never reachable from the internet, and only receives snapshots that
# fabloom-verify uploads. The JSON and LZ4 inputs these CVEs concern come from that one
# trusted client, not from visitors. Recorded 2026-10-23.

# jackson-core 2.22.1 (fixed in 2.22.3)
CVE-2026-89407
CVE-2026-89425
# jackson-databind (fixed in 2.22.2 / 2.22.3)
CVE-2026-68497
CVE-2026-91776
CVE-2026-91777
# lz4-java 1.11.2 (fixed in 1.11.4)
CVE-2026-106451
# guava 33.6.0-jre (fixed in 33.7.2): memory exhaustion while deserializing, the same class
# as the jackson entries and fed by the same single client. Added to Trivy's database on
# 2026-10-27; recorded the same day.
CVE-2026-102554
